AUDIO: 'The trick here is simple. You just zoom in slightly on your clip, enough to push the watermark corner outside the visible frame. Since Flow tends to place its watermark in a fixed spot near the edge, a small zoom is often all it takes to crop it'

[02:27] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: The Canva online editor interface, with the video playing after the zoom adjustment.
AUDIO: 'out completely. This will not work perfectly for every single shot, especially if your framing is already tight. But for most clips, a slight zoom is genuinely enough, and it takes seconds instead of minutes.'

